<%#
    For pages that measure nothing for OneUptime: status pages and public
    dashboards, which belong to OneUptime's customers and whose visitors are
    not OneUptime's to measure, and the admin console.

    Common/Utils/Analytics.ts reads this flag before it starts product
    analytics (PostHog), so include it in <head>, before the app's bundle.
    These pages load no Google tag either: never include AnalyticsConsent.ejs
    alongside it.
-%>
<script>
    window.oneUptimeProductAnalyticsDisabled = true;
</script>
